From: omaflake contributors
Subject: cocoa: a window per further display

A GPU with several outputs (virtio-gpu max_outputs=N) has a graphic console
per output. The main window shows the first; each further one gets a window
of its own (2D, CGL and ANGLE/EGL), opened on the screen of its number when
there is one, that can be moved and made full screen like the main one. A
shown window connects its output: the guest gets a monitor of the window's
size, with its suggested position right of the ones before it. Closing the
window disconnects the output; View -> its console shows it again.

The pointer stays the one USB tablet: positions from every window are mapped
onto the guest's whole desktop, the displays side by side in output order
(the guests' default layout). Keys reach the guest from every window. With a
single output nothing changes except that the main window tracks the pointer
while the app is active (not only while it is the key window).

